  "groups": [
    {
      "id": "gleich",
      "regel": [
        "Many short words come in two forms: with a written accent and without one. **The accent changes the word**: *é* = is, *e* = and; *à* = to the, *a* = the.",
        "In the plural, the verbs *ter* and *vir* get a circumflex: *ele tem, eles têm*; *ele vem, eles vêm*.",
        "*há* (there is, ago) has an accent, *a* (to, the) has none. *por* is the preposition, *pôr* the verb to put."
      ],
      "regelTr": {},
      "title": "Sounds the same, spelt differently",
      "lead": "In fast speech the difference is small or easy to miss. In writing you see it at once.",
      "pairs": [
        {
          "id": "e-e",
          "level": "A1",
          "a": {
            "w": "é",
            "pos": "verb: is",
            "ex": "O Rui <b>é</b> professor."
          },
          "b": {
            "w": "e",
            "pos": "conjunction: and",
            "ex": "O Rui <b>e</b> a Ana são professores."
          },
          "why": "é with an accent is the verb ser: he/she is. e without one means and.",
          "tr": {},
          "check": {
            "gap": "A minha irmã ___ médica.",
            "options": [
              "é",
              "e"
            ],
            "answer": "a"
          },
          "variety": "pt-PT"
        },
        {
          "id": "a-a",
          "level": "A1",
          "a": {
            "w": "à",
            "pos": "a + a (the): to the",
            "ex": "Vou <b>à</b> farmácia."
          },
          "b": {
            "w": "a",
            "pos": "preposition or article",
            "ex": "Vou <b>a</b> Lisboa. Dou <b>a</b> chave à Ana."
          },
          "why": "à is the preposition a joined with the article a: a + a = à. Before a name or a noun without an article, or before a verb, you write a: vou a Lisboa, vou a pé, começo a trabalhar.",
          "tr": {},
          "check": {
            "gap": "Vou ___ escola de autocarro.",
            "options": [
              "à",
              "a"
            ],
            "answer": "a"
          },
          "variety": "pt-PT"
        },
        {
          "id": "ha-a",
          "level": "A1",
          "a": {
            "w": "há",
            "pos": "verb: there is, ago",
            "ex": "<b>Há</b> uma farmácia aqui perto?"
          },
          "b": {
            "w": "a",
            "pos": "preposition: in (time) to",
            "ex": "Daqui <b>a</b> dois dias estou em casa."
          },
          "why": "há (with an accent) is the verb haver: there is, or ago (há dois anos). Without the accent, a looks ahead: daqui a dois dias.",
          "tr": {},
          "check": {
            "gap": "Moro em Lisboa ___ três anos.",
            "options": [
              "há",
              "a"
            ],
            "answer": "a"
          },
          "variety": "pt-PT"
        },
        {
